AudioNodeInput took the single-connection fast path for every node, handing it the
connection's own bus; WebKit takes it only for a node whose channel count follows
its inputs (channelCountMode max). A node with an explicit or clamped count (the
destination, a recorder, a stream destination, a panner) so received whatever count
its one input carried, unmixed: a recorder that had seen stereo then recorded a later
mono input in its first channel only. The fast path is WebKit's again, and the
summing bus, sized to the computed count, mixes each connection as the node
interprets its channels rather than always as speakers.

